 release success is claimed. 17.l.W/10.15.9 adds complete passive merge preparation for local, Git, Baseline and complete bundle sources, public merge.plan and native Work. Direct and partitioned results retain original plan bytes, source/history/build bindings, exact metadata, native target validation and full target bytes. All global phases survive real checkpoints; final delivery independently recomputes from sealed originals. Source-path changes never silently rebind a passive snapshot. Negative targets remain negative and cannot authorize writes. Public CLI binding, Code 8 progress, Code 1 fail-on-change, cancellation, source overlap rejection and rehashed intermediate-result rejection receive real behavior tests. No behavior test was run in Dev; stage-specific Apply evidence is required. 17.l.R supplies the public merge plan --for-apply / merge apply bridge over the existing complete native ChangePlan, receipt, backup and writer. Small complete native four-source variants cover equivalent actual merged target bytes, argv/structured calls, direct/resumed/portable preparation, native dry-run with no writes, historical request replay after later changes, missing/negative current host authority and refused stale or tampered input. Public portable Work covers every global boundary without old source paths, exact noncanonical resolution/audit originals, rehashed phase rejection and incomplete/foreign runtime/input closure. C centralizes the matrix with unchanged oracles. No new writer or authority bypass; native recovery/current Evidence/review/code-source cases remain required. Dev performs only static checks and collection. Successful stage gates and M17 full-suite/platform evidence must be read from their actual Apply results."},"preconditions":["Owned nine-artifact corpus with ordered document occurrences, external identities, two bound attachment payloads, a configuration artifact and synthetic hash-bound relation review; no real approval is claimed.","Owned explicit parsed artifact candidates from real CSV, NDJSON, ReqIF and ReqIFZ codecs; supplied mappings and complete creation envelopes; retained synthetic relation review with native status checks; explicit trusted test-host gates and publication authority. No authentic human approval is claimed.","Complete actual source backup, explicit original native plan/report and external bindings; full target bytes, genuine host semantic services and no invented authority."],"primary_verification_id":"SR-VER-0021","required_environment":{"declared_minimum_python":"3.10","implementation":"cpython","measured_scope":"current-run-only"},"requirement_id":"SR-REQ-0285","resources":{"harness_suite_timeout":null,"harness_test_timeout":null,"owned_temporary_files":true},"specification_sha256":"5b930634203407b577c21108e7e329b8e0fe1616727dc8cd92e1cc201d3e90aa","steps":["Export and decode the corpus with the existing NDJSON envelope and explicit per-type CSV profiles; reconstruct only decoded artifacts and transported attachment bytes and compare native semantic model roots.","Export and decode the declared ReqIF/ReqIFZ scalar/XHTML intersection; compare native/external identities, mapped values, ordered occurrence identities, the addresses relation and complete attachment bytes.","Assess the retained native review with the real relation-status service; require current only for the unchanged relation and both endpoint contexts, with approval_granted=false.","Require explicit whole-record losses for review/configuration/evidence outside the chosen ReqIF intersection and reject fail_on_loss for remaining native-resource or format losses.","Modify the source context, target context or relation of a transported review and require suspect; replace its relation identity or omit its review and require unreviewed, with approval_granted=false.","Persist all candidate units and the final whole-target reduction in real Work checkpoints, reopen after each window and compare exact canonical ImportPlan bytes to the single-run planner across all four formats, two resource profiles and three window sizes.","Execute both plans through the existing native import writer with current inputs and explicit live authority; compare actual target bytes, semantic roots, audit operations, all four literal object values and the retained suspect review.","Require complete object coverage after relocation and loss of the original source, no rerun of completed mapping kernels, original late-error contracts, preserved durable generations on checkpoint failure and refusal of inconsistent or incomplete evidence.","Build actual Core and PYZ distributions, resume each Work unit in a fresh process after moving distribution and Work directories, and require identical completed planning results without live project writes or inferred authority.","Recompute the full planning/loss report and target model from original source bytes; verify every source/target byte, current native model and unchanged historical original/hash closure.","Observe a real completed native migration with verified receipts; reject stale or incomplete targets, extra files, unsafe paths, active recovery and tampered bindings/reports without writes.","Resume every native source/plan/verification phase through actual Work checkpoints and hash-bound external packages into a new sandbox and process; compare full results with direct execution.","Reject forged phases/completion, changed runtime, missing source/backup/authority and interrupted checkpoints; preserve the confirmed prefix or return a concrete blocker.","Publish one final actual native migration transaction with fresh live checks, then prove historical request replay and explicit recovery after interruption."],"test_case_format_version":1,"test_case_id":"SR-TC-0285","test_ids":["tests/test_format_roundtrips.py::test_native_intersection_preserves_full_corpus_and_current_review[False-de-DE-csv]","tests/test_format_roundtrips.py::test_native_intersection_preserves_fu